<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="bl-bean" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title></title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>Black Bean Soup</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>1 \frac{1}{2}</m> cups dried black beans (or 15 oz. can, not dried)</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 celery ribs, chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>3 medium carrots, chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 large onion, chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 garlic cloves, minced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 teaspoons olive oil</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>6 \frac{1}{2}</m> cups broth</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon dried oregano</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon dried thyme</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> teaspoon cayenne pepper</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 bay leaf</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 tablespoons lime juice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup sour cream or plain yogurt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup minced fresh cilantro (garnish)</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Place beans in a large saucepan; add water to cover by 2 in.  Bring to a boil; boil for 2 minutes.  Remove from heat; cover and let stand for 1 to 4 hours or until beans are softened.  Drain and rinse beans, discarding liquid.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a Dutch oven, saute the celery, carrots, onion, and garlic in oil patiently.  Add the beans, broth, oregano, thyme, salt, cayenne, and bay leaf.  Bring to a boil.  Reduce heat; cover and simmer for 1 to <m>1 \frac{1}{4}</m> hours or until beans are tender.  Discard bay leaf.  Cool slightly.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a blender, cover and process soup in batches until smooth.  Return to pan; heat through.  Stir in lime juice.  Garnish each serving with sour cream or yogurt and cilantro.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>